<article class="env-definition" id="02QP">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/02QP">Definition <span data-tag="02QP">42.7.6</span>.</a> Let $(S, \delta )$ as in Situation <a href="/tag/02QL" data-tag="02QL">42.7.1</a>. For any scheme $X$ locally of finite type over $S$ and any irreducible closed subset $Z \subset X$ we define </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  \dim _\delta (Z) = \delta (\xi )  \]
</div>
  <p> where $\xi \in Z$ is the generic point of $Z$. We will call this the <em>$\delta $-dimension of $Z$</em>. If $Z$ is a closed subscheme of $X$, then we define $\dim _\delta (Z)$ as the supremum of the $\delta $-dimensions of its irreducible components. </p>
</article>